;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljk:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; Three independent authorities are cited, not one: GLEIF (the global LEI
;; system), Colombia's Registro Unico Empresarial y Social (RUES, the national
;; commercial register the Camaras de Comercio administer, republished on
;; Colombia's national open-data portal), and Ecuador's Servicio de Rentas
;; Internas (SRI, the national tax authority). The second and third are not
;; picked because they happened to agree -- they are the registration
;; authorities GLEIF itself names on this entity's children, reached by
;; following GLEIF's own RA pointers.
;;
;; Two joins are load-bearing and are checkable only against those authorities'
;; own bodies:
;;
;;   * NIT 900102580-3. GLEIF lists Alicorp Colombia S.A.S among this LEI's
;;     direct children and records it as validated at RA000101 under that id.
;;     RA000101 resolves, at GLEIF, to the Bogota Chamber of Commerce. Asked for
;;     NIT 900102580, Colombia's RUES returns ALICORP COLOMBIA S.A.S and gives
;;     its chamber as BOGOTA -- so the parent-child edge and the chamber GLEIF
;;     names are both corroborated by a register that does not source them from
;;     GLEIF.
;;
;;   * RUC 0992711523001. GLEIF lists Inbalnor S. A. (EC) as a direct child,
;;     validated at RA000691, which GLEIF resolves to Ecuador's SRI. Asked for
;;     that RUC, the SRI returns INBALNOR S.A., status ACTIVO, principal
;;     activity "fabricacion de alimentos preparados para animales acuaticos"
;;     -- aquafeed, which is the business line Alicorp runs through Vitapro.
;;     The SRI is a tax authority; it has no LEI field and no view of GLEIF.
;;
;; WHY STATUS ALONE CANNOT CARRY THESE ROWS. Measured 2026-08-20, each authority
;; answers 2xx for a WRONG identifier:
;;   * RUES with nit=900102581 -> HTTP 200, body "[]"
;;   * SRI with ruc=0992711523002 -> HTTP 204, empty body
;;   * SRI with ruc=1790016919001 -> HTTP 200, a different real company
;;   * GLEIF filtered by registeredAs=20100055238 -> HTTP 200, "total":0
;; So for every one of these rows it is the substring, not the HTTP status,
;; that is doing the work. That is the property the gate exists to hold.
;;
;; IDENTITY ROWS vs ATTRIBUTE ROWS. Not every row discriminates on its own,
;; and pretending otherwise would be the same dishonesty as trusting the status
;; code. Measured by mutation on 2026-08-20, repointing all 31 subject-record
;; URLs at a real sibling LEI (VITAPRO S.A., 549300U4HYYWKC16GO36) made 24 rows
;; DRIFT and left 7 standing: corroboration level, registration authority
;; RA000689, jurisdiction PE, region PE-CAL, status ISSUED, and the two managing
;; LOU rows. All seven are true of that sibling too. They are ATTRIBUTE rows --
;; they say what is true of the entity the URL names, and they mean something
;; only because the IDENTITY rows in the same block pin which entity that is.
;; The gate still fails as a whole, which is the property that matters; this
;; note exists so no reader mistakes an attribute row for an identification.
;;
;; The Ecuadorian block was rewritten after this measurement. Its status and
;; classification rows originally matched bare field values, and a swap to
;; CORPORACION FAVORITA -- also ACTIVO, also a SOCIEDAD -- left them standing.
;; Both now match a run that includes the name or the RUC, so all five SRI rows
;; DRIFT together on any swap. The Colombian block already had this property:
;; RUES answers an unknown NIT with an empty array, so nothing survives.
;;
;; ENCODING. Substrings are chosen from the RAW response body, and the two
;; hosts do not agree on how to encode Spanish. api.gleif.org escapes all
;; non-ASCII as \uXXXX (it publishes "Cámara de Comercio de Bogotá"
;; and "ALICORP HOLDCO ESPAÑA SL"), while datos.gov.co and the SRI emit
;; UTF-8 directly. Rather than write backslash escapes into this file, the
;; GLEIF rows match a pure-ASCII run of the same field -- hence
;; " Chamber of Commerce" (from internationalOrganizationName) rather than the
;; accented local name. A normalised form would hide which body was read.
;;
;; The two PKRY rows match "country":"Peru" and "status":"ACTV" rather than the
;; legal-form name because GLEIF's own ELF table spells it "Socieda Anonima
;; Abierta" -- missing the final d of "Sociedad". That typo is GLEIF's, it is
;; live today, and matching it would make this catalog fail the day GLEIF fixes
;; it for a reason that has nothing to do with this entity.
;;
;; Deliberately NOT cited, and why (all measured 2026-08-20):
;;
;;   * SUNAT e-consultaruc.sunat.gob.pe -- the register GLEIF names as having
;;     validated the SUBJECT's own RUC 20100055237, and so the citation this
;;     catalog would most like to have. A GET returns the search form (22,835
;;     bytes) and nothing else; the RUC is submitted by POST behind a session,
;;     and the delivered body contains neither "20100055237" nor "ALICORP".
;;     Appending accion/nroRuc/tipo query parameters returns the same form,
;;     byte for byte. There is no substring a body check could honestly assert,
;;     so the subject's RUC is cited from GLEIF's registeredAs/validatedAs
;;     fields and is NOT claimed to have been re-checked at SUNAT.
;;   * SMV (Superintendencia del Mercado de Valores), Peru's securities
;;     regulator, which Alicorp files with as a listed issuer. www.smv.gob.pe
;;     301-redirects to www.gob.pe/smv; that body is 276,713 bytes and contains
;;     zero occurrences of "Alicorp". The per-issuer paths under /SIMV/ and
;;     /ConsultasP8/ answer 403 to automated clients.
;;   * BVL (Bolsa de Valores de Lima). /emisores/detalle?companyCode=ALICORC1
;;     answers 200 but renders via JavaScript; stripped of markup the delivered
;;     body reads "Bolsa de Valores de Lima" and nothing more.
;;   * Chile's CMF and SII (www.cmfchile.cl, zeus.sii.cl) and Ecuador's
;;     Superintendencia de Companias (mvs.supercias.gob.ec) -- DNS does not
;;     resolve for these hosts from the environment this gate runs in. That is
;;     a reachability fact about the gate, not a judgement about the registers.
;;   * Spain's Registro Mercantil. registradores.org is reachable but entity
;;     lookup is session-gated, and the BOE's open BORME API answered 400/404
;;     for the sumario dates tried. Locating the ALICORP HOLDCO ESPANA SL entry
;;     needs a publication date this catalog does not have, so the Spanish
;;     child is cited from GLEIF only.
;;   * The legal representatives. Both the SRI and RUES rows above carry a
;;     natural person's name AND their national identity number. No claim in
;;     this catalog needs them, so none is cited and none is reproduced here.
;;   * www.alicorp.com.pe is the company's own site, not a register, and is
;;     not cited for any claim here. Note also that this repository does NOT
;;     currently hold an archived Alicorp privacy policy, whatever
;;     80-data/public/tos.journal.edn labels itself: the document captured
;;     there on 2026-07-25 carries the marker "404 | Alicorp Consent Details",
;;     and the URL it came from still answered HTTP 404 on 2026-08-20. The
;;     capture is faithful -- its recorded sha256 matches its recorded text --
;;     but it is a 404 page. See the README.
;;
;; Independent third-party archive. Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
;; sponsored by ALICORP SAA.

